---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import StructureFacts from "../../components/StructureFacts.astro";
import SetStructureDemo from "../../components/SetStructureDemo.astro";
import TermCallout from "../../components/TermCallout.astro";
import { gSetTerm } from "../../lib/atlas/standalone-terms";
import "../../styles/set-lesson.css";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="GSet"
  description="Alice starts the ranger's trail-beacon survey with an add-only replicated set."
  territory="Structures"
  sheetTitle="GSet"
>
  <article class="set-lesson">
    <header class="page-intro">
      <p class="territory-label">Structures</p>
      <h1>GSet</h1>
      <p class="structure-summary">
        The ranger sends Alice, Bob, and Carol onto separate trails to list
        every beacon they find. Their first rule is simple: names can enter the
        survey, but they never leave.
      </p>
    </header>

    <StructureFacts
      family="CRDT"
      model="State-based grow-only set"
      updates="Add only"
      merge="Take the union of all known members."
      delivery="Safe under repeated and out-of-order delivery"
      bestFor="Permanent records of values that never need removal"
      cost="One retained entry for each distinct member"
    />

    <section aria-labelledby="first-beacon-title">
      <h2 id="first-beacon-title">Alice reports Eagle Creek</h2>
      <p>
        Alice finds the Eagle Creek beacon and adds its name to her notebook.
        Bob and Carol are out of radio range. They still have empty lists.
      </p>
      <p>
        A <dfn><a href="/glossary/#gset">GSet</a></dfn> only adds members.
        When the hikers exchange their notebooks, each replica keeps the union
        of every name it has seen.
      </p>
      <TermCallout {...gSetTerm} />
      <figure>
        <table aria-label="Eagle Creek GSet delivery">
          <thead>
            <tr><th scope="col">Moment</th><th scope="col">Alice</th><th scope="col">Bob</th><th scope="col">Carol</th></tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><th scope="row">Alice reports</th><td>Eagle Creek</td><td>empty</td><td>empty</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">Report arrives</th><td>Eagle Creek</td><td>Eagle Creek</td><td>Eagle Creek</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">Old copy repeats</th><td>Eagle Creek</td><td>Eagle Creek</td><td>Eagle Creek</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
        <figcaption>Union keeps one member even when Alice's report arrives more than once.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <pre aria-label="GSet merge rule"><code>local members ∪ remote members</code></pre>
    </section>

    <SetStructureDemo
      kind="g-set"
      title="Combine the hikers' reports"
      description="Alice and Bob report different beacons while Carol waits. Exchange the records and watch every notebook keep the same union."
      rule="Keep every distinct reported name."
      raceLabel="Race Alice and Bob's reports"
    />

    <section aria-labelledby="gset-limit-title">
      <h2 id="gset-limit-title">Then the ranger needs an active list</h2>
      <p>
        Alice returns to Eagle Creek and finds that the old beacon has been
        taken down. The ranger no longer wants a record of every beacon ever
        observed. The ranger needs the beacons that are active now.
      </p>
      <p>
        A GSet cannot express that change. Removing the name locally would not
        be monotonic, and Carol's delayed copy could restore it. The next set
        adds permanent removal evidence instead of deleting history.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="notes-title">
      <h2 id="notes-title">Sources and implementation</h2>
      <p>
        Watershed's{" "}
        <a href="https://github.com/tylerbutler/watershed/blob/4a8739323ee491f353fcaa8ccfb0488419c1cd43/src/watershed/g_set_kernel.gleam">GSet kernel</a>
        {" "}uses set union for confirmed, optimistic, and peer-to-peer state.
      </p>
    </section>

    <nav class="structure-next" aria-label="Continue through set structures">
      <a href="/structures/sets/">Back to set family</a>
      <a href="/structures/two-p-set/">Continue to TwoPSet</a>
    </nav>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
